5) Main Limitations: 
    The current communication uses HTTP. For a more scalable IoT system, MQTT could be used because it is lighter and better for real-time device monitoring.
    The API key is currently assumed to be stored in firmware. A better production design would use secure provisioning, unique credentials per device, HTTPS, and possibly certificate-based authentication.
    The analog voltage calculation assumes a 3.3V reference. For higher accuracy, the ADC should be calibrated.

6) Steps to build, flash, and test the firmware:
      Install ESP-IDF and set up the development environment.
      Create a new ESP-IDF project or open the existing firmware project.
      Place the firmware code in the main source file, usually main.c.
      Update the configuration values:
            Wi-Fi SSID
            Wi-Fi password
            HTTP endpoint URL
            Device ID
            API key
            GPIO pins if the wiring is different
      Connect the hardware:
            Analog sensor output to GPIO34 or the selected ADC pin
            Digital sensor output to GPIO27
            Status LED to GPIO2
            Common GND between ESP32, sensors, and power supply
            Sensor outputs limited to 3.3V maximum
      Build the project using:
            idf.py build
            Connect the ESP32 to the computer using USB.
            Flash the firmware using:
            idf.py -p COM_PORT flash
      Open the serial monitor using:
            idf.py -p COM_PORT monitor
            Check that the ESP32 connects to Wi-Fi successfully.
            Verify that sensor readings appear every 5 seconds.
            Confirm that after 5 readings, the firmware calculates the average and sends the payload to the HTTP backend.
            Test failure handling by turning off Wi-Fi or disconnecting the backend. The firmware should store failed readings in the offline queue.
            Restore Wi-Fi or backend access and confirm that the firmware retries and sends stored readings.
            Check the status LED behavior:
            Slow blink while connecting
            Solid ON when connected
            Fast blink on error
